<section class="content-section content-section--tint"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading-page"><p class="section-kicker">START WITH THE PROBLEM</p><h2>A product is a starting point—not a forced fit.</h2><p>We help clarify whether a ready-made product, configuration, integration or custom build is the most practical approach.</p></div><div class="page-grid"><article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">A</span><h3>Describe the workflow</h3><p>What is happening today, where is the friction, and who needs to use the solution?</p><a href="/contact/">Talk it through <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article><article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">B</span><h3>Understand constraints</h3><p>Consider devices, connectivity, data, integrations, permissions and rollout.</p><a href="/contact/">Discuss requirements <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article><article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">C</span><h3>Plan a realistic path</h3><p>Prioritise the most valuable first stage and leave room for improvement.</p><a href="/services/">Explore delivery <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article></div></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="page-cta"><div><h2>Let’s solve the right problem.</h2><p>Tell us what your team needs to improve and we can discuss the available options.</p></div><a class="button button--primary" href="/contact/">Start a Conversation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>

<section class="content-section content-section--tint"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading-page"><p class="section-kicker">HOW TO CHOOSE A SOLUTION</p><h2>Match software to the workflow, not the other way around</h2><p>A practical solution starts with the process, people and information involved. The product or development approach comes after the requirements are understood.</p></div><div class="page-grid"><article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">01</span><h3>Standardise a repeatable task</h3><p>When a workflow is common and stable, a ready-made product may provide a sensible starting point.</p><a href="/products/">Compare VYQDA products ↗</a></article><article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">02</span><h3>Connect systems and information</h3><p>Where data is re-entered or hand-offs are unclear, review integration opportunities and ownership of each record.</p><a href="/services/">Explore development services ↗</a></article><article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">03</span><h3>Support a unique process</h3><p>If the workflow is distinctive, assess whether custom software or a phased extension is justified.</p><a href="/contact/">Discuss a use case ↗</a></article></div></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><div class="wrap page-split"><div><div class="section-heading-page"><p class="section-kicker">FROM WORKFLOW TO IMPLEMENTATION</p><h2>Define success before choosing features.</h2><p>Clear acceptance criteria help keep a business software project focused and make it easier to evaluate whether the solution actually improves the work.</p></div></div><ol class="page-list"><li><span>01</span><div><strong>Document the current process</strong><p>Capture the normal flow, exceptions, approvals, and the people responsible for each step.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><strong>Identify the outcome to improve</strong><p>Choose a useful measure such as fewer duplicate entries, clearer records or less time spent preparing a report.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><strong>Check fit and constraints</strong><p>Review security, permissions, devices, integrations, data migration and how the work should continue during rollout.</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><strong>Plan adoption and support</strong><p>Include staff onboarding, ownership, issue reporting and post-launch improvement in the plan.</p></div></li></ol></div></section>
